AN ORDINANCE REGARDING ELECTION PROCEDURES FOR THE TOWN OF PINE MOUNTAIN

BE IT ORDAINED, by the Mayor and Town Council of the Town of Pine Mountain, Georgia, and it is hereby ordained, by the authority of the same as follows;

SECTION I: DATE OF ELECTIONS A. The general municipal elections shall be held biennially on the Tuesday next following the first Monday in November; B. Special elections shall be held in odd numbered years only on 1. The third Tuesday in March; 2. The third Tuesday in June; 3. The third Tuesday in September; or 4. The Tuesday after the first Monday in November. C. Special elections shall be held in even numbered years only on 1. The date of the general primary; 2. The third Tuesday in September; or 3. The Tuesday after the first Monday in November. D. The provisions of this Section shall not apply in the event of a recall election or to fill a vacancy of office.

2:
SECTION III; NOTICE OF CANDIDACY A. Each candidate shall file notice of candidacy in the office of the Municipal Election Superintendent at least 22 but not more than 52 days prior to the election. B. The next succeeding day may be substituted for Saturday, Sunday, or holiday as last day to exercise any privilege. C. Each candidate shall accompany his or her notice of candidacy with an affidavit stating: 1. The candidate’s residence, with street number, if any, and his or her post office address;

- 2. That the candidate will have continuously resided in the Town of Pine

Mountain for a period of twelve (12) months as of the date of the election in which the candidate is seeking office;

The candidate’s profession, business, or occupation, if any;

- 4. That the candidate is a qualified elector of the municipality and is eligible to vote in the election in which the candidate is seeking office;

