DUTIES OF THE GOVERNING AUTHORITY: The governing authority shall exercise all powers and duties imposed by this ordinance which shall include the following:

A. To budget and appropriate annually the funds it shall deem necessary for the conduct of the elections;

B. To provide by purchase or rental the necessary number of voting machines, tabulating machines, and/or vote recorders.

C. To select the superintendent, registrars, deputy registrars, poll officials, and other employees necessary to hold an election;

D. To furnish the proper election officials all blank forms, including tally and return sheets, for use in all municipal elections; and such forms shall have printed thereon appropriate instructions for their use;

F. To prepare and publish all notices and advertisements which may be required by law in connection with the conduct of elections.

6:
Qualification of electors shall be:

A. Must be registered as an elector;

B. Must be a citizen of the United States;

C. Must be a resident of The Town of Pine Mountain;

D. Must be 18 years of age or older; E. Must not have been judicially determined to be mentally incompetent; F. Must not have been convicted of a felony involving moral turpitude; and G. Must be possessed of all other qualifications prescribed by law. SECTION VIII: SPECIAL ELECTIONS:

All general or special elections or primaries conducted in the Town of Pine Mountain shall be held in compliance with and pursuant to the provisions of the Georgia Election Code and this Ordinance.
